.TH SACDFS\-CTL 8 "" "sacdfs" "System Administration"
.SH NAME
sacdfs\-ctl \- start and stop sacdfs safely on a NAS without systemd
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B sacdfs\-ctl
.RB { start | stop | status | restart }
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B sacdfs\-ctl
starts
.BR sacdfs (1)
in the foreground under
.BR setsid ,
records its process ID, and stops it with SIGTERM and a wait, never with SIGKILL, which would
leave a dead mount. It needs only a POSIX shell (BusyBox ash is enough), and is meant for the
start\-up hook of a NAS.
.PP
It reads its settings as NAME=value lines and never runs them as shell code. A value may be in
single quotes (\(aqR&B\(aq, with \(aq written as \(aq\e\(aq\(aq), in double quotes without $ or a
backquote, or bare. Run as root, it refuses a settings file, a program or its own file that a
user other than root could change or replace, because root runs them.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B start
Mounts the images on the mount point. Clears a leftover dead sacdfs mount first, and refuses a
mount point that holds another filesystem.
.TP
.B stop
Sends SIGTERM and waits (see
.BR SACDFS_STOP_WAIT ).
.TP
.B restart
.B stop
and then
.BR start .
.TP
.B status
Says whether sacdfs is running.
.SH SETTINGS
Read from
.I /etc/default/sacdfs
(the RPM package:
.IR /etc/sysconfig/sacdfs ),
or from the file named by the environment variable
.BR SACDFS_CONF .
The same file is read by the packaged systemd unit.
.TP
.B SACDFS_IMAGES
The image file, or the folder of images (SOURCE).
.TP
.B SACDFS_MOUNT
The mount point.
.TP
.B SACDFS_OPTIONS
More options for
.BR sacdfs (1),
separated by spaces.
.TP
.B SACDFS_INDEX_CACHE
The folder of the seek index, for hosts where a start\-up hook has no HOME. Passed as
.BR \-\-index\-cache .
.TP
.B SACDFS_BIN
The program (default
.IR /usr/local/bin/sacdfs ,
.I /usr/bin/sacdfs
in packages).
.TP
.B SACDFS_PIDFILE
Default
.IR /var/run/sacdfs.pid .
.TP
.B SACDFS_LOG
Where the log goes; default
.IR /var/log/sacdfs.log .
.TP
.B SACDFS_STOP_WAIT
Seconds to wait for sacdfs to exit after SIGTERM; default 30. It waits longer if
.B SACDFS_OPTIONS
sets a larger
.BR \-\-stop\-grace .
.SH "EXIT STATUS"
.TP
.B 0
Done, or running.
.TP
.B 1
Failed.
.TP
.B 2
Usage error.
.TP
.B 3
Not running (\c
.BR status ).
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /etc/default/sacdfs
.TQ
.I /etc/sysconfig/sacdfs
The settings.
.TP
.I /var/run/sacdfs.pid
.TQ
.I /var/log/sacdfs.log
The default process ID file and log.
.SH EXAMPLES
A settings file:
.PP
.RS
.nf
SACDFS_IMAGES=/volume1/music
SACDFS_MOUNT=/volume1/sacd
SACDFS_OPTIONS="\-\-allow\-other"
.fi
.RE
.PP
Then:
.PP
.RS
.nf
sacdfs\-ctl start
sacdfs\-ctl status
sacdfs\-ctl stop
.fi
.RE
.SH "SEE ALSO"
.BR sacdfs (1),
.BR sacdfs\-nfs (1)
